From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:53:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(bootstrap): use space-efficient Darwin malloc for servers
 [daveey]

libmalloc reads MallocSpaceEfficient only at process start. Set it at the
managed interpreter exec, or re-exec once from bootstrap for in-place
server relaunches. Scrub Hermes-owned variables after exec so agent child
commands keep their default allocator; preserve operator values and an
environment-only opt-out. Share the existing server argv predicate.

Register the new stdlib bootstrap module in the startup syntax inventory.
No gateway restart or delivery is part of this change.

Proof (Linux, patched/passed platform; native footprint effect untested):
RED on parent 542663b487e8efb79038bcc834593ecc72a00608, new test file only:
  hermes-core-wt test tests/hermes_cli/test_launch_malloc_env.py
  7 failed in 0.99s; all seven fail importing absent launch_malloc.
GREEN after implementation:
  test_launch_malloc_env.py (7 passed)
  Required seven existing regression files pass unchanged (90 passed).
  Expanded run: 14 files, 1514 passed, 0 failed, 1 Windows-only skipped,
  95.5s. Includes venv_sync consumers, startup syntax inventory and
  subprocess encoding/environment guards.
  scripts/check: 20 checks ok before main advanced; final gate reruns on
  rebased head through canonical ship.

The live macOS footprint effect belongs to the separate measurement card;
these tests establish environment plumbing only.
